## Applications

Each application starts from a minimal skeleton that already passes its own quality gates. Run the commands from the application directory.

| Application | Gates |
|---|---|
| `apps/backend` (Python) | `uv sync --frozen`, `uv run ruff format --check .`, `uv run ruff check .`, `uv run mypy src`, `uv run lint-imports`, `uv run pytest tests/unit --cov`, `uv run pytest tests/integration` |
| `apps/backend` (C#, .NET 10 SDK) | `dotnet restore --locked-mode`, `dotnet format --verify-no-changes`, `dotnet build -warnaserror --no-restore`, `dotnet test tests/App.UnitTests -p:CollectCoverage=true --no-restore`, `dotnet test tests/App.IntegrationTests --no-restore`, `dotnet test tests/App.ArchitectureTests --no-restore` |
| `apps/frontend` (React, TypeScript; Node 20 or newer) | `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, `pnpm format:check`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test:unit --coverage`, `pnpm test:integration`, `pnpm exec playwright install chromium` (once), `pnpm e2e` |

A technology that has no skeleton in the templates only has its `README.md`.

The skeletons use fixed names (distribution `backend` and `frontend`, Python package `app`, C# solution and root namespace `App`) and the lockfiles `uv.lock`, `pnpm-lock.yaml` and the `packages.lock.json` of every C# project are committed. To refresh them:

- Backend (Python): `uv lock --upgrade`, then `uv sync` and run the gates.
- Backend (C#): raise the versions in `Directory.Packages.props`, run `dotnet restore --force-evaluate`, then `dotnet restore --locked-mode` and run the gates.
- Frontend: raise the versions in `package.json` (keep them compatible with Node 20), run `pnpm install --lockfile-only`, then `pnpm install` and run the gates.

Check the locked dependencies for known vulnerabilities with `uv export --frozen --no-hashes --no-emit-project | uvx pip-audit -r /dev/stdin --disable-pip --no-deps` (Python backend), `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` (C#; it exits 0, read its output) and `pnpm audit --audit-level high` (frontend).

